            "known-failures": {
                "F-03 tables with attributes are preserved verbatim": "core/html on 6.1 re-serializes its content through a DOM, so a <table> without an explicit <tbody> is regenerated with one and the block is reported as containing unexpected content. The content itself is intact and the block still renders; the editor shows a resolve prompt. Normalizing the markup first would fix the notice and break the verbatim preservation that Custom HTML exists for, so it is recorded rather than papered over.",
                "module et_pb_map with a pin": "Same core/html re-serialization on 6.1: an empty <p> is dropped by the DOM round trip. Same trade-off, same decision."
            }
